# Ship the signed wireless regulatory database into the initramfs.
#
# cfg80211 requests regulatory.db during kernel_init (before rootfs is
# mounted).  On this device the rootfs is f2fs on sda16, mounted by the
# initramfs at ~1.77 s, while cfg80211 asks at ~0.50 s -- so /lib/firmware
# does not exist yet and the request fails with ENOENT:
#
#   [0.499820] cfg80211: Loading compiled-in X.509 certificates ...
#   [0.507939] faux_driver regulatory: Direct firmware load for
#              regulatory.db failed with error -2
#   [0.516325] cfg80211: failed to load regulatory.db
#
# Without it cfg80211 stays in the world domain (country 99), where the whole
# 5 GHz band is PASSIVE-SCAN: 5 GHz AP mode is refused
# ("regulatory prevented using AP config, downgraded") and the handset's own
# 5 GHz traffic runs under a domain that only permits passive reception.
#
# The db is small (6 KB) and signed, so adding it to the initramfs is cheap.
#
# Format: one absolute path per line (mkinitfs files-extra syntax).

/lib/firmware/regulatory.db
/lib/firmware/regulatory.db.p7s
